 run it  there are a couple of online  publications but they are increasingly  difficult for people to access because  the consumer authority which has been  given  almost unlimited  ability to block access to various  resources has blocked access to them  which makes them very difficult to edit  in addition to being very difficult to  read right because you can't access the  back end any easier than the front end  one of the  uh there was a very good and very big  online publication called lentaru which  was  basically uh  purged last year so its former  editor-in-chief has gone into exile and  is running a russian language  publication from riga  in latvia  with a small editorial editorial staff  in riga and a lot of reporters based on  the ground  in russia and it's quite good  but i think that uh you know and it's it  it's another heroic effort  it's really sad that uh  that the most important online  publication is now  now has to be run from exile and of  course  the moment will come when the consumer  third will block access to it  question over here on the right  yes oh thank you um recently at the  meeting with  mikhail kadarkovsky and  somebody asked towards the end so he  never really had a chance to answer  mr kardarkowski if everything will work  out as you hope and we hope what will  you do with 87 percent  so  just as one author that i recently read  calls it a golog of russian mind  russian people's minds go lag  what do you think is putting the problem  or this gulag of russian mind  that didn't hasn't leaved itself out yet  is the problem because it seems that  this country keeps on choosing  the monsters to lead them  you know i think russia is a country  that has been  taking  an incredible amount of abuse over the  last century  and when we talk about individuals who  have been abused we never expect them to  heal themselves and start being normal  all of a sudden uh for some reason when  we talk about an entire society that has  been abused we 