 um there's a great  documentary about this  uh community called children 404.  we're going to take one last question i  just want to invite everybody out to the  atrium immediately after the program  where masha is going to be signing books  thanks everybody  thank you  masha in a man without a face you write  about two horrendous terrorist attacks  in russia one was the apartment house i  think it was moscow and the other attack  was on a school outside of moscow  hundreds of children were killed  you conclude that the soviet excuse me  the russian security services were  responsible my question is this do you  think putin was involved or responsible  or was it a rogue action of extreme  elements in the fsb yeah i actually  don't think that the school attack was  uh was organized by the fsb i think the  school attack is much more sort of along  classic uh  lines of of a rogue terrorist  organization  uh but what happened was that in the end  during the uh  the so-called liberation attempt  uh de facto the fsb the russian secret  police and the terrorists were  were working in concert  because the fsb was working to uh  whether by design or by you know their  general ethos  was working to maximize bloodshed and  the number of casualties  um  now as with the apartment building  bomber bombings in uh  in august september 1999  um  there's a lot of evidence that points to  the fsb i would stop short of saying  that i came to the conclusion that it  was the fsb because i don't have enough  information and that's the problem  with being a journalist especially being  a journalist in a country where  none of the law enforcement agencies or  the civil oversight agencies do their  jobs i mean  um  maybe there are amazing investigative  journalists out there who can crack a  mystery like that all on their own i  don't think that's possible uh i think  we will you know journalists lack the  tools for that uh i can't collect enough  evidence i can write about what's out  ther